  <prompt>H11UserProvisioningHandler.cs is ALREADY REAL per DS-4 ('✅ REAL -- Graph REST provisioner + B2B invitation + consent verifier'). The ONLY blocker is C5.8's Graph app-role grants (User.ReadWrite.All, User.Invite.All etc. per DS-5 §C5.8) for the L2 UAMI, delivered by task 111. This task performs LIVE VERIFICATION against a dev target that H11's user-provisioning flow (NativeAccount and B2BGuest branches per design D6) function correctly now that the grants exist.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in Graph REST user provisioning, B2B guest invitation flows, and consent-gate verification against a live tenant.</role>

  <goal>A live verification run confirms H11's user-provisioning collaborators function correctly for BOTH the NativeAccount and B2BGuest identity-preset branches (per design.md D6) against a dev target, now that the L2 UAMI holds the necessary Graph grants (User.ReadWrite.All, User.Invite.All). The B2B consent gate is confirmed to correctly produce a WaitingOnGate outcome when consent is pending (external, session-free wait), not a false Pass.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>DS-4 §2 (H11 row): '✅ REAL -- Graph REST provisioner + B2B invitation + consent verifier. ~0 code. C5.8 grants (User.ReadWrite.All, User.Invite.All etc.). Tests exist.' DS-2b §1.2 notes H11's wall-clock includes '3-10 min (+ B2B consent gate for that preset)' -- confirming the consent-gate branch is a real, externally-latent path this verification must specifically exercise, not skip.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/services/Sprk.Provisioning.ControlPlane.Core/Handlers/UserProvisioning/H11UserProvisioningHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="new">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/h11-live-verification-2026-08.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="111" status="pending">The C5.8 Graph grants for the L2 UAMI must exist</dependency>
      <dependency task="143" status="pending">Sequenced after H10's live verification per the Dataverse chain's DAG order (H10 -&gt; H11)</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec.md FR-38">L2's admin-env Dataverse credential model is Path X: L2 UAMI registered as a Dataverse Application User via DefaultAzureCredential pinned to the UAMI (DS-8). MUST NOT provision a new client-secret for L2. The Dataverse-ClientSecret KV secret itself MUST NOT be deleted (BFF still consumes it) -- only L2's dependency on it is removed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="DS-4 §2 H11 row">This is VERIFICATION, not re-implementation -- document any deviation found rather than silently patching.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>H11 live verification (post C5.8)</topic>
    <files>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/design.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds4-handler-audit.md</file>
      <file>projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/design-study-ds2b-concurrency-safety-deep-dive.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Rigor + load">Emit RIGOR LEVEL (FULL). Read H11UserProvisioningHandler.cs's existing implementation + design.md D6's identity-preset branching in full.</step>
    <step order="1" name="Confirm grants">Verify the L2 UAMI holds User.ReadWrite.All + User.Invite.All (task 111's C5.8 grants) before proceeding.</step>
    <step order="2" name="NativeAccount branch">Live-invoke H11 with a NativeAccount preset against a dev target; confirm a real user is provisioned via Graph REST.</step>
    <step order="3" name="B2BGuest branch">Live-invoke H11 with a B2BGuest preset; confirm a real invitation is sent and the consent verifier correctly produces WaitingOnGate for pending consent (not a false Pass).</step>
    <step order="4" name="Report">File a verification report documenting both branches' live outcomes.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If EITHER identity-preset branch fails live verification, STOP and escalate — DS-4's fully-real classification makes any live failure a signal that either task 111's grant scope is wrong or the classification needs correction.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the B2B consent verifier reports Pass for a genuinely-pending consent (a false positive), STOP immediately and escalate as a HIGH-severity finding — this is exactly the consent-gate-advances-on-fiction class of defect this project's whole H13 acceptance-gate rebuild exists to eliminate (per DS-4's H3 finding of the same class).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <tools>
    <tool name="az account">get-access-token for live verification</tool>
    <tool name="dotnet">test (existing suite re-run)</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="report">projects/customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1/notes/h11-live-verification-2026-08.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A live NativeAccount-preset invocation of H11 against a dev target succeeds -- a real Graph user is provisioned.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A live B2BGuest-preset invocation succeeds -- a real invitation is sent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The consent verifier correctly reports WaitingOnGate (not Pass) for a genuinely-pending B2B consent.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A verification report exists in notes/ documenting both branches' live outcomes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">H11's existing test suite (per DS-4, already passing) continues to pass unmodified.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- H11's Graph REST provisioner, B2B invitation flow, and consent verifier are ALREADY fully implemented per DS-4's audit. Extension -- N/A, this is verification. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- without live verification, a false-Pass consent-gate defect (the same class DS-4 found in H3) could ship undetected into Wave G-7's acceptance run, where it would be far more expensive to diagnose.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>

  <notes-completion date="2026-08-20">
    Live verification of H11's 3 REST/Graph seams (GraphRestUserProvisioner, GraphRestB2BInvitationClient,
    GraphRestB2BConsentVerifier). The consent verifier (fully read-only, the escalation-trigger-relevant
    seam) was fully live-verified end-to-end -- both Verified and Pending branches -- via new durable
    xUnit smoke tests (H11SeamsSmokeTests.cs) run genuinely live in-sandbox (unlike H10's equivalent
    tests, which soft-skipped). The two WRITE-capable seams (POST /users, POST /assignLicense, POST
    /invitations) had their REST shapes ground-truthed against Microsoft Learn (exact field-name match);
    the actual writes are deferred to live-ceremony (real Entra user creation / real invitation email --
    no safe automated undo), same precedent as task 143 (H10).

    BONUS CATCH (MAJOR, fixed same commit): cross-referencing GraphRestB2BInvitationClient's POST
    /invitations against Microsoft Learn's own least-privileged-permission table found the pre-existing
    14-role GraphAppRoles.cs / L2GraphAppRolesRegistry.cs catalog (task 005) was missing User.Invite.All
    entirely -- once task 111's C5.8 grants are live-executed, every B2BGuest-preset H11 run would have
    received a permanent 403 on the invitation POST. Fixed by adding a 15th catalog role (GUID
    ground-truthed live: 09850681-111b-4a89-9bed-3f2cae46d706), mirrored to L2, with every stale "14"
    reference across 8 files (+ spec.md FR-33 + the customer deployment guide) updated. Mirror-parity
    test (L2GraphAppRolesRegistry_MirrorsBffGraphAppRolesConstant) re-confirmed byte-identical post-fix.

    Consent-verifier reuse check (CLAUDE.md §11): confirmed H11's GraphRestB2BConsentVerifier (checks a
    guest user's externalUserState) and H3's GraphAdminConsentVerifier (checks app-registration
    oauth2PermissionGrants) answer genuinely different questions against different Graph resources -- no
    consolidation opportunity; H11 correctly owns its own verifier.

    Deferred, documented (not fixed): H11UserProvisioningOptions has zero Bicep wiring and its
    AccountDomain default ("spaarke.onmicrosoft.com") is the Spaarke tenant's own domain, not a
    customer's -- assessed as fail-loud (Graph rejects an unverified UPN domain), not fail-silent, but a
    genuine deployment-completeness gap. Recommended as a follow-up task; out of proportion to this
    verification-scoped task's boundary.

    Escalation triggers: both cleared. Trigger 1 (branch failure) did not fire -- the one genuine defect
    found was a catalog-completeness gap, fixed in-commit per task 143's own precedent, not a live
    orchestration failure. Trigger 2 (false-Pass on pending consent) was directly tested and NOT
    observed -- the Pending-branch smoke test proves an unknown/unaccepted guest id is never reported as
    Verified.

    Tests: 1003 -> 1005/1005 (+2, H11SeamsSmokeTests.cs). Full report: notes/h11-live-verification-2026-08.md.
  </notes-completion>
</task>
